      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The park’s tallgrass prairie restoration began in 1939, making it the oldest in the National Park Service.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/home/learn/historyculture/index.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Heritage Center, shaped like a plow breaking the land, overlooks 100 acres of restored prairie.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/home/learn/historyculture/index.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1971, the Freeman School, an original one-room prairie schoolhouse, was added to the park.",
